e  passengers stranded i've had to rebook  my  reservations for like four or five times  doctors warn things will get worse  predicting another post-holiday blizzard  of covid 19 cases i don't think you're  going to start to see a national peak  until we get into february because  there's parts of the country that really  haven't been hard hit by omicron yet and  the virus will spread around the country  americans are now starting 2022 the  third year of the pandemic with record  numbers of new cases rising  hospitalizations and essential workers  pushed to the limit again  jennifer johnson global news washington  here in canada winter weather has caused  hundreds of canceled flights in the last  week flying can already be stressful  especially during a pandemic and when a  teenager is traveling alone and is  forced to sleep overnight at an airport  departure gate it compounds the  frustration that's what happened to a 16  year old and her powerless mother ross  lord explains  being at the mercy of an airline can be  a downer as grace rowe learned while  flying alone on westjet from saskatoon  to halifax trouble with connecting  flights forced her to sleep overnight at  a departure gate i try to be like well  you know  just make the best of it  even though it's a terrible situation  and  and  i thought she was holding it together  pretty well after being delayed leaving  edmonton grace says she scrambled to  change planes in toronto she was turned  away at the gate then along with other  frustrated passengers her flight to  halifax was pushed back by more than 16  hours because i checked just because i  was looking to see what gate i'd be at  in toronto and i saw that it moved my  flight to 4 pm the next day  tempers boiled over  together passengers were more frustrated  by the airline's confusing explanations  the west just sent an email saying the  staffing issue and now when the  passenger just wants a hotel all of a  sudden they blame it on the weather that  rin