vering the person  climbed a tall barbed wire fence around  6 40 p.m local time their fate  citizenship and motive is unknown though  reports suggest it was a civilian not a  soldier since the late 1990s more than  34 000 north koreans have defected to  the south but crossings in the other  direction are extremely rare  ahead sudan's prime minister steps down  after two more people are killed in  pro-democracy protests  there is a major political development  in sudan tonight the recently reinstated  prime minister has resigned abdullah  hamdak says there needs to be a new  agreement struck with the military in  order for the country to transition to  democratic rule he had returned to his  post just six weeks ago after he was  detained when the military seized  control of the country in october  earlier today at least two people were  killed in and around the capital  khartoum when security forces cracked  down on protesters who were demanding an  end to military involvement in the  country's government  after team canada brought home the gold  medal in women's soccer at the tokyo  olympics last summer 2022 could be  another historic year our men's national  team is in contention to qualify for its  first fifa world cup in 36 years the  tournament takes place in november in  qatar but the tiny gulf nation is under  scrutiny thousands of immigrant workers  have reportedly died during the enormous  construction project there others have  faced brutal working conditions as  redmond shannon reports some of the  teams going to qatar will be taking a  stand to highlight the issue  canada's 2-1 win over mexico in freezing  edmonton made canada's soccer fans  believe  believe that their team can get to a  world cup played in the desert heat  when the tiny gulf nation of qatar was  awarded the tournament there were  questions about the bid process and  about how a country the size of cape  breton island could host such a large  event  armies of construction workers from  so