ind  themselves used as political pawns by a  country intent on destabilizing the eu  we are like a ball like a ball in the  stadium  belarus and poland  they kick us  in france some migrants risk everything  to try and reach the uk  in the pursuit of a better life dozens  of migrants died crossing the english  channel in november in the worst  disaster on record this disaster  underscores how dangerous it is to cross  the channel in this way united nations  says 166 people have died that way since  2014. i think the question is how do you  get how do you create enough control  of the flows that are out there we must  transcend the immunity of our societies  against the vitals of hate the un  believes that in 2022 nearly 275 million  people will require humanitarian  assistance and protection  a task too great for any individual  nation a u.n agreement in 2018 saw 164  countries sign onto a pac to better  address migration the u.s wasn't  involved at the behest of then-president  donald trump migration is part of a  smart economic policy it's part of you  know it's part of population growth it's  part of of  learning and innovation diffusion of  ideas but you you start to to give it  some sort of form so that people feel  like there's a plan there that this is  not an army marching  north but rather a set of people who  were welcoming in  because they can become part of our  society that challenge will require  countries to work together to find a  solution we've been frozen in this  political debate where you have these  side two sides who can't find any  compromise and the stakes couldn't be  higher any crisis from natural disaster  to war could upend best laid plans at a  time when millions of people are already  risking everything in search of a better  life  reggie chikini global news washington  and that is global national for this  sunday night i'm nitu garcia tonight  your canada is a frozen boundary bay in  delta bc we'd love to see your corner of  the coun